        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "6U1Rq",
          "name": "Article Body",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "fill": "$bg-white",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "padding": [
            80,
            120
          ],
          "alignItems": "center",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "PUhMP",
              "name": "bodyInner",
              "width": 720,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 24,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "YWlw3",
                  "name": "bodyP1",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "I stood at the southern terminus monument, my pack heavy on my shoulders, staring north into the desert. The morning air was cool but I could already feel the promise of heat in the sun climbing above the hills. Behind me, the metal border fence stretched east and west. Ahead, 2,650 miles of trail.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.8,
                  "fontFamily": "Source Serif 4",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "YvezT",
                  "name": "bodyH2",
                  "fill": "$text-primary",
                  "content": "The Weight of Beginning",
                  "fontFamily": "Source Serif 4",
                  "fontSize": 28,
                  "fontWeight": "600",
                  "letterSpacing": -0.5
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "1sqRE",
                  "name": "bodyP2",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "There's something surreal about starting a journey this long. You've planned for months — gear lists, resupply boxes, training hikes — and then suddenly you're just... walking. One foot in front of the other. The trail doesn't care about your spreadsheets.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.8,
                  "fontFamily": "Source Serif 4",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "EENHH",
                  "name": "blockquote",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "stroke": {
                    "thickness": {
                      "left": 4
                    },
                    "fill": "$burnt-orange"
                  },
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "padding": [
                    0,
                    0,
                    0,
                    24
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "Ed4Be",
                      "name": "bqText",
                      "fill": "$text-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "&quot;The trail provides.&quot; I'd heard this phrase a dozen times in planning. Today, standing at mile zero, I chose to believe it.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.8,
                      "fontFamily": "Source Serif 4",
                      "fontSize": 18,
                      "fontWeight": "normal",
                      "fontStyle": "italic"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "0EqFB",
                  "name": "bodyP3",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "The first water source was 20 miles away. I'd cached water at Lake Morena, but between here and there was nothing but chaparral, rocky switchbacks, and the kind of quiet that makes you hear your own heartbeat. My legs felt strong. My spirit felt ready. I took my first step north.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.8,
                  "fontFamily": "Source Serif 4",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "vVDNp",
                  "name": "divider",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 1,
                  "fill": "$border-subtle"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "DrH3h",
                  "name": "bodyP4",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "By noon I'd covered eight miles and found shade under a scrubby oak tree. I ate a tortilla with peanut butter and watched a lizard do push-ups on a rock. This is the kind of lunch meeting I can get behind. The desert was alive — birds calling, insects humming, the wind carrying the scent of sage.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.8,
                  "fontFamily": "Source Serif 4",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
