                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "QU7zq",
                  "name": "vP1",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Day three started with one of the most incredible sunrises I've ever seen. The desert sky lit up in bands of orange, pink, and purple as I packed up camp near Hauser Creek. In today's video, I share the raw beauty of those first trail mornings and what it feels like to truly wake up with the land.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.8,
                  "fontFamily": "Source Serif 4",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "GcECg",
                  "name": "vP2",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "The hiking itself was challenging — steep climbs out of creek valleys, loose rocky trail, and the beginning of real desert heat. But there's a rhythm forming now. Walk, rest, eat, walk. My body is starting to understand what my mind committed to months ago.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.8,
                  "fontFamily": "Source Serif 4",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
