              "name": "sec4title",
              "fill": "#FFFFFF",
              "content": "\"Near Finish\" Email Sequence (Final 200 Miles) — BUILT",
              "fontFamily": "Source Serif 4",
              "fontSize": 24,
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "ezlek",
              "name": "sec4desc",
              "fill": "#FFFFFFAA",
              "content": "COMPLETED:\n\n• 3-email sequence triggered at mile 2450, 2550, and 2650:\n  1. \"200 Miles to Go\" — Paul enters Washington. Last chance to increase. Gradient hero.\n  2. \"100 Miles to Go\" — The final push. Explains what happens when Paul finishes (honor process).\n  3. \"Paul Made It to Canada!\" — Celebration + \"HONOR MY PLEDGE\" CTA linking to /honor page.\n• Each sent only once (Redis set: emails:near_finish:sent)\n• Replaces standard milestone emails for those distances\n• Tone shifts: informational → preparatory → celebratory + action-oriented\n• Finish email includes final pledge total, 50/50 split, and direct honor link\n• New email template: sendNearFinish() with 3 variants in src/lib/email.ts",
              "fontFamily": "Source Serif 4",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
